        "title": "feat(ios): redesign Talk call UI and Voice & Talk settings",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- Move Talk entry from the tab bar into Chat and refresh the call screen with a WeChat-style light layout, wallpapers, and no in-call dock.\n- Add customizable accent colors and reorganize Voice & Talk settings rows, typography, and picker labels.\n- Hide tab bar on Voice & Talk pages and simplify the connecting state by removing agent name and status text.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe iOS Talk experience exposed call controls and Voice & Talk settings in inconsistent places, with the Talk surface competing with the main tab model. This PR moves Talk into the Chat flow, refreshes the call UI, and gives users focused settings for accent color and call background without leaving stale in-call controls in settings.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `pnpm native:i18n:check` -> `native-app-i18n: entries=2384 changed=false`\n- `pnpm lint:swift` -> completed with no serious violations; the previous `TalkBackgroundSettingsView.swift` design-token error is gone.\n- `IOS_DEST='generic/platform=iOS Simulator' pnpm ios:build` -> `** BUILD SUCCEEDED **` locally with Xcode 26.4.\n- Manual flow checked during development: Chat -> Talk, connecting/connected/offline states.\n- Manual settings checked during development: Settings -> Voice & Talk, wallpaper and accent color pickers.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `xcodebuild` Debug build for iPhone simulator\n- [x] `OpenClawBrandTests` and `TalkProStateTests`\n- [x] Manual: Chat -> Talk, connecting/connected/offline states\n- [x] Manual: Settings -> Voice & Talk, wallpaper and accent color pickers",
